meta {
  name: 02-ReadSubmitterProfile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/users/{{ownerSubmitterId}}/profile
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Before I approve anything I want to look at WHO submitted. The persona
  # doc says "read submitter context".

  Problem: `GET /users/{id}/profile` returns the *public* profile —
  `PublicUserProfile`. Same fields any logged-in stranger would see:
  fullName, displayName, role, identityVerifiedAt, suspended, joinedAt,
  averageRating.

  As an admin I need MORE than the public profile to make a verification
  decision:
  - Email (so I can spot disposable-domain patterns)
  - Phone
  - All previous verification submissions and their decisions
  - Whether this user has ever been suspended (and why)
  - Whether this user has ever been reported

  None of that is exposed. I'm being asked to approve identity badges
  using a profile card the public could read. That's backwards.
}
